            "review_title": "Review at Truong Tho Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Brownsjo\nOttawa, Canada55 contributions\n0\nTraditional Vietnamese food. Specializes in pigeon and other uncommon items.\nJan 2016 • Couples\nStumbled upon this local place, when wooden doors opened. Located across from newly opened club on Ta Hien street. Helpful that they have a translated version of types of food available, We saw other patrons eating what we thought was quail but identified it was pigeon, hence the name of the restaurant. Very tasty with the adjoining salt and lime. Also ordered plump shrimp in flour batter, similar to tempura. Due to the French inspired name the menu includes frog, rabbit, snails, etc when available. For Hanoi not cheap but worth the price. Our meal for two was about $25 USD for two dishes plus a small soup, rice and two beers.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 31, 2016",
